= CRANIX Introduces CranixNotes with a Built-in Grade Manager =

'''Cranix-Solutions announces CranixNotes, a new module in the CRANIX that turns everyday notes into structured communication — and gives teachers a full Grade Manager to record, weight and review the grades of every student directly on their device.'''

<code>[CITY], [DATE]</code> — Cranix-Solutions today announced the release of '''CranixNotes''' in the CRANIX (version <code>[VERSION]</code>). The component combines a contextual note system with a powerful grading engine, so the same tool teachers already use to communicate with classes and parents also serves as their grade book.

== Notes that do more than inform ==

CranixNotes is available from any object list in the app via '''⋮ Actions → Write Note'''. Whether it is a single student, an entire class, a device or a room, users write the note exactly where the context already exists — no switching tools, no re-entering recipients.

The module distinguishes between general communication and student-related records. General notes (generic, to-do) can be sent to individuals or whole groups, while user-related note types cover exactly the cases schools deal with every day: performance, grading, lateness and excused or unexcused absence.

== The Grade Manager at the centre ==

The standout capability of CranixNotes is the '''Grade Manager (NotenManager)'''. It lets authorised users manage the grades of individual students in a structured, traceable way:

* '''Per-student grading''' — Each grade note records the teaching subject and subject area, the grade value, a weighting and a free-text comment.
* '''Weighted grades''' — The weighting field allows different assessments to count differently, reflecting how schools actually calculate final marks.
* '''Bulk entry for a whole class''' — When opened on a group, the Grade Manager presents every student in one table. Teachers enter grades and comments for the entire class in a single pass instead of switching between records.
* '''Subject-aware''' — Grades are tied to the teaching subject and its subject areas, so entries stay meaningful and easy to filter.
* '''Full history''' — Every entry is stored with its type, creator and timestamp, and can be filtered, reviewed, edited or deleted afterwards.
* '''Access-controlled''' — Editing follows the existing CRANIX permission model (<code>note.manage</code>, <code>crxnote.manage</code>), and teachers automatically retain control over the entries they created themselves.

== Bringing order to school communication ==

Beyond grading, CranixNotes gives schools a single, consistent channel for communication:

* '''Contextual notes''' — Start from any list; recipients are pre-filled from the current selection, group, lesson or event.
* '''Multiple note types''' — Generic, to-do, performance, grading, lateness and excused/unexcused absence, plus access notes for devices and institute objects.
* '''Filtering''' — Notes are grouped by type and sorted by date, so the latest information is always on top.
* '''Reminders''' — A reminder date can be attached to a note so nothing is forgotten.
* '''Role-aware editing''' — Administrators can manage everything; teachers can create new notes and edit their own; students only read.
* '''Built on a clean API''' — Notes are managed through the CRANIX <code>/crxNotes</code> interface with create, update, filter and delete operations.

== Benefits for schools ==

For teachers, CranixNotes means one place for both communication and grades — a class list becomes a grade book in a few taps, and a comment to a student becomes a documented record. For school administrators, it means grade-related information follows the same permission and audit model as the rest of the CRANIX platform, rather than living in spreadsheets on individual devices.

== Availability ==

CranixNotes is available now in the CRANIX  It appears in the app for users whose roles include the corresponding note permissions; no separate installation is required.

== About Cranix-Solutions ==

Cranix-Solutions develops CRANIX, a comprehensive open platform for the administration of schools and educational institutions — covering users, devices, rooms, software and much more. The CRANIX extends this platform to smartphones and tablets as a Progressive Web App.

